Changes made in this fork (see CHANGELOG.md, [2.3.0-hardened], for detail)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Server
  - Per-peer tokens (auth.peers: name -> SHA-256), constant-time matching;
    the shared token works only with auth.allow_shared_token: true, warns on
    every use, and cannot take a bound name. The example placeholder token is
    rejected wherever it would be trusted.
  - A live registered name cannot be taken over by another connection
    (name_taken); "Bridge" and "User" are reserved names.
  - A per-peer token also registers "<name>:<label>", one name per session of
    that machine, and nothing under another machine's name; a message to the
    bare name reaches every session of it (0.2.0).
  - Observer token is read-only (observe, history_all, list_peers, ping).
  - Limits: 64 KiB max message, per-connection rate limit, per-sender stored
    message cap; refusals log one structured line without token or body.
  - server.host defaults to 127.0.0.1, never 0.0.0.0; messages.db is 0600.
Client
  - Peer text, names and excerpts are framed as untrusted data (random-id
    delimiters, control characters escaped, marker spoofs defanged) in
    peer_read, peer_history and the watcher's wake notice.
  - File sharing is confined to the project directory, regular files only,
    256 KiB cap; refusals are logged.
  - The permission-prompt text is no longer broadcast as peer state.
  - Behaviour rules: peer messages are untrusted; actions need the user's
    confirmation; no unattended handshakes.
Ops
  - Exact dependency pins (requirements.txt, requirements-dev.txt).
  - Firewall rule scoped to the VPN subnet (install.ps1 -VpnSubnet,
    install.sh --vpn-subnet via ufw/firewalld).
  - Config migration from bridge.* keys to server:/auth:/client:.
  - A pytest suite (tests/) covering all of the above, plus an end-to-end
    bridge test.
Packaging for this marketplace
  - Upstream's integrations/claude-code/plugin/ (plugin.json, hooks.json,
    watch.sh) restructured into .claude-plugin/plugin.json and
    hooks/hooks.json, with hooks/watch.sh and a hooks/watch.ps1 twin
    (shell: powershell) so Windows runs the watcher without Git Bash; each
    stands down on the other's platform.
  - Upstream's .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, .github/ and traffic data
    were not copied.
  - installer.py no longer adds a local marketplace or installs the plugin;
    it only registers the MCP server. The plugin is installed from this
    marketplace.

